# the build sees only what the image ships: everything else here is the comic library, a working folder,
# or files that are not part of the program. every file is named, rather than matched, so a stray script
# beside them never ends up in a published image
*
!requirements.txt
!mirror_base.py
!chapters.py
!update_comics.py
!adopt_comic.py
!web_ui.py
!web_page
!comiclib
comiclib/**/__pycache__
# the reader's image (reader/Dockerfile), built from here so it can take comiclib. its web page is built
# inside the image, so neither a local build nor node_modules is sent
!reader/requirements.txt
!reader/comicreader
!reader/web
reader/**/__pycache__
reader/web/node_modules
reader/web/dist
